AniList identity mapping
-----------------------
Public cross-reference data is fetched on demand from Fribb/anime-lists
(https://github.com/Fribb/anime-lists).
No copy of the full dataset is bundled with Kinos. Public anime metadata is
queried from AniList (https://anilist.co); Kinos is not affiliated with AniList.

Startup sounds
--------------
assets/sounds/intro_clap.wav is cut from "VideoTronic Super 8mm Projector"
by ajoyce86 (https://freesound.org/s/213741/).
assets/sounds/intro_bed.ogg mixes "MUSCChim_Atonal Crystal Chime Texture 1_EM"
by newlocknew (https://freesound.org/s/772279/) with "Singing Bowl, long
without reverb" by hollandm (https://freesound.org/s/573805/), low-passed and
kept far below.
assets/sounds/intro_celesta.ogg is made from "Celesta Chime Descending" by
Qvantor (https://freesound.org/s/879801/): slowed and given a reverb.
All four are released under Creative Commons 0 (public domain dedication),
https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/; they were trimmed,
faded and level-adjusted for Kinos.

Wrapped music
-------------
The yearly Wrapped plays music by Kevin MacLeod (incompetech.com), licensed
under Creative Commons: By Attribution 4.0 License,
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/:
assets/sounds/wrapped_piano.ogg is "Feather Waltz",
assets/sounds/wrapped_tension.ogg is "Division",
assets/sounds/wrapped_ampleur.ogg is "Five Armies",
assets/sounds/wrapped_melancolie.ogg is "Sad Trio",
assets/sounds/wrapped_legerete.ogg is "Easy Lemon".
They were level-matched, given short fades in and out, and converted to
Ogg Vorbis for Kinos; the music itself is unchanged.
